course: dictionary
lesson: 2806
title: Dissatisfied and the prefix dis-
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dissatisfied means not pleased or not happy, because something was not as good as you hoped or expected. The word has parts: dis- means not, and satisfied means pleased. So dissatisfied means not pleased.
explain: Look at the clues around it. A dissatisfied customer complains or wants their money back. People also say dissatisfied with something, as in «She felt dissatisfied with the slow service.» The words after it tell you what caused the feeling.
explain: Spelling is tricky. «That one rule explains the famous double letters.» Dis- plus appear gives disappear, with one s, because appear has no s. But dis- plus satisfied gives dissatisfied, with two s's, because satisfied starts with s. Mis- plus spell gives misspell, also with both s's.
fact: Dissatisfied means not pleased, because something was not as good as you hoped or expected.
fact: The prefix dis- means not, so dis- + satisfied = dissatisfied.
fact: A dissatisfied customer complains or wants their money back.
fact: «Dissatisfied» has two s's, because «satisfied» starts with an s.
fact: Other prefixes that mean not: il- in «illegal», ir- in «irregular», and im- in «immature».
exercise: What does dissatisfied mean? | Lost in a big crowd | *Not pleased, because something was not as good as you hoped | Very excited and full of joy
exercise: How many s's are in dissatisfied? | Three | *Two | None | One
exercise: In «illegal», which prefix means not? | pre- | re- | ex- | *il-
test: The shopkeeper said, «The customer was dissatisfied with the slow service.» What does dissatisfied suggest? | *Not pleased with the service | Hungry and tired | Very tall | Happy and thankful
test: Which word has two s's? | dislike | *dissatisfied | disappear | disagree
exam: Dissatisfaction is a noun. Which word is the verb that means to make someone not pleased? | satisfied | dissatisfied | dissatisfaction | *dissatisfy
